asr-000060
00:07:28.319 --> 00:07:34.639
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: Good afternoon, Honorable Albert Garcia, Senior Vice Chair, and Honorable Members of the House

asr-000061
00:07:34.639 --> 00:07:36.365
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: Committee on Appropriations.

asr-000065
00:07:37.520 --> 00:07:43.440
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: We begin this briefing by recalling the mandate that guides the work of the Philippine Charity

asr-000066
00:07:43.440 --> 00:07:44.400
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: Sweepstakes Office.

asr-000067
00:07:44.400 --> 00:07:49.759
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: The Philippine Charity Sweepstakes Office is the principal government agency for raising

asr-000068
00:07:49.759 --> 00:07:55.680
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: and providing funds for health programs, medical assistance and services, and charities

asr-000069
00:07:55.680 --> 00:08:02.560
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: of national character, through the holding and conduct of sweepstakes horse races, lotteries,

asr-000070
00:08:02.560 --> 00:08:05.039
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: and similar activities.

asr-000071
00:08:05.039 --> 00:08:12.479
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: This mandate is at the heart of every peso that PCSO generates and every peso that we allocate.

asr-000072
00:08:12.479 --> 00:08:18.960
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: Our financial performance is therefore not only about revenues, expenditures, and targets.

asr-000073
00:08:18.960 --> 00:08:26.319
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: It is ultimately about our capacity to provide meaningful assistance to the Filipino people.

asr-000074
00:08:26.319 --> 00:08:37.919
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: Let us now proceed to the budgetary highlights and major thrusts, including plans, programs, and strategies to be undertaken by the PCSO in 2027.

asr-000075
00:08:37.919 --> 00:08:49.040
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: First is the distribution of landing craft vessels, or LCVs, to coastal provinces and provinces with coastal municipalities.

asr-000076
00:08:49.040 --> 00:08:55.120
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: This initiative aims to address the unique challenges faced by geographically isolated

asr-000077
00:08:55.120 --> 00:09:02.560
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: and coastal communities, particularly in accessing health care and emergency services.

asr-000078
00:09:02.560 --> 00:09:17.120
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: Second, the donation of medical equipment to beneficiary entities. This is intended to strengthen the capacity of hospitals and health care facilities by providing much-needed equipment.

asr-000079
00:09:17.120 --> 00:09:25.440
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: The desired impact is improved healthcare, better patient care, and greater access to essential medical services.

asr-000080
00:09:25.440 --> 00:09:33.680
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: Third, PCSO's participation in the government initiative to establish a radiation oncology center.

asr-000081
00:09:33.680 --> 00:09:40.560
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: This initiative seeks to improve access to cancer diagnosis, treatment, and specialized care,

asr-000082
00:09:40.560 --> 00:09:46.800
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: while helping reduce the financial and health burdens of cancer on Filipino families.

asr-000083
00:09:46.800 --> 00:09:54.399
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: Fourth, increasing PCSO revenues through the development of new games and betting platforms.

asr-000084
00:09:54.399 --> 00:09:55.279
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: This is critical.

asr-000085
00:09:55.279 --> 00:10:01.200
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: to sustaining PCSO's capacity to fund its various health and charitable programs.

asr-000086
00:10:01.200 --> 00:10:07.519
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: By responsibly expanding our revenue-generating activities and responding to changing consumer

asr-000087
00:10:07.519 --> 00:10:12.880
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: preferences, we aim to increase the resources available for medical assistance,

asr-000088
00:10:12.880 --> 00:10:20.560
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: health programs, and other charitable initiatives. Finally, strengthen public service delivery

asr-000089
00:10:20.560 --> 00:10:27.040
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: through digitalized processes and the successful transfer of operations to the PCSO Corporate

asr-000090
00:10:27.040 --> 00:10:35.040
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: Center in San Marcelino, Manila. Digitalization is intended to make our services more accessible,

asr-000091
00:10:35.040 --> 00:10:38.480
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: efficient, transparent, and responsive. At the same time,

asr-000092
00:10:38.480 --> 00:10:44.959
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: the successful transfer to the corporate center will provide a more integrated and efficient

asr-000093
00:10:44.959 --> 00:10:49.600
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: environment for our operations. Next slide, please.

asr-000094
00:10:49.600 --> 00:10:51.040
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: For our operational

asr-000095
00:10:51.040 --> 00:11:00.240
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: highlights from 2024 to 2026. First, the Medical Assistance Program remains one of PCSO's most

asr-000096
00:11:00.240 --> 00:11:06.160
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: significant and direct expressions of its mandate to provide meaningful medical assistance to

asr-000097
00:11:06.160 --> 00:11:15.920
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: Filipinos in need. From 2024 to the first semester of 2026, PCSO provided 8.13 billion in assistance

asr-000098
00:11:15.920 --> 00:11:29.600
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: to 681,999 beneficiaries. In 2024, PCSO assisted 326,482 beneficiaries with 3.24 billion.

asr-000099
00:11:29.600 --> 00:11:41.839
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: In 2025, despite a 28% decline in beneficiaries to 236,217, assistance slightly increased to 3.25

asr-000100
00:11:41.839 --> 00:11:49.360
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: billion. This translates to a substantial increase in average assistance per beneficiary, reflecting

asr-000101
00:11:49.360 --> 00:11:53.920
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: PCSO's focus on greater efficacy and efficiency.

asr-000102
00:11:53.920 --> 00:11:58.160
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: The focus is not merely on the number of beneficiaries served, but

asr-000103
00:11:58.160 --> 00:12:04.480
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: on maximizing the impact of every peso allocated to medical assistance.

asr-000104
00:12:04.480 --> 00:12:14.240
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: This is particularly significant given PCSO's continuing contribution to government's health agenda, including its increased remittance to

asr-000105
00:12:14.240 --> 00:12:15.120
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: the universal

asr-000106
00:12:15.120 --> 00:12:18.320
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: health care program. Despite this higher

asr-000107
00:12:18.320 --> 00:12:26.000
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: financial obligation to broader national health system, PCSO continues to provide substantial

asr-000108
00:12:26.000 --> 00:12:34.000
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: direct assistance to patients and their families. Moreover, pursuant to the expressed desire

asr-000109
00:12:34.000 --> 00:12:38.000
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: of the members of the House Committee on Appropriations,

asr-000110
00:12:38.000 --> 00:12:45.920
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: PCSO has expanded its financial assistance to include professional fees for qualified patients.

asr-000111
00:12:45.920 --> 00:12:57.279
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: This makes the assistance more comprehensive, responsive, and patient-centered, helping families meet the full cost of necessary medical care.

asr-000112
00:12:57.279 --> 00:13:14.800
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: Next, the Institutional Partnership Program shows a positive trend, with beneficiaries doubling from 19 in 2024 to 38 in 2025, accompanied by an increase in assistance from 12 million to 24.6 million.

asr-000113
00:13:14.800 --> 00:13:22.240
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: By the first semester of 2026, another 19 beneficiaries had already been assisted.

asr-000114
00:13:22.240 --> 00:13:29.040
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: A particularly strong growth is seen in the Medical Transport Vehicle Donation Program.

asr-000115
00:13:29.040 --> 00:13:43.200
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: Beneficiaries increased from 431 in 2024 to 1,090 in 2025, while assistance increased from 913.7 million to 2.48 billion.

asr-000116
00:13:43.200 --> 00:13:44.079
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: This reflects

asr-000117
00:13:44.079 --> 00:13:52.160
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: PCSO's intensified efforts to bring emergency and medical transport services closer to communities.

asr-000118
00:13:52.160 --> 00:14:06.800
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: As of July 31, 2026, PCSO has distributed 154 PTVs to complete the 100% distribution of PTVs in provinces, cities, and municipalities.

asr-000119
00:14:06.800 --> 00:14:19.440
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: The Medical Equipment Donation Program, on the other hand, shows increased assistance funding from 20.5 million in 2024 to 22 million in 2025 and

asr-000120
00:14:19.440 --> 00:14:31.440
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: already reached 154.58 million in the first semester of 2026, indicating a significant acceleration in equipment support.

asr-000121
00:14:31.440 --> 00:14:45.440
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: Meanwhile, the Outpatient Services and Multi-Specialty Clinic continues to expand its reach, with beneficiaries increasing from 7,383 in 2024 to 9,416

asr-000122
00:14:45.440 --> 00:14:55.519
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: in 2025 and another 8,440 beneficiaries already served in the first half of 2026.

asr-000123
00:14:55.519 --> 00:15:01.600
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: For the financial highlights for 2024 to the first semester of 2026,

asr-000124
00:15:01.600 --> 00:15:10.399
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: PCSO's total revenues from its major games increased by 4.02 percent from 62.35 billion

asr-000125
00:15:10.399 --> 00:15:23.839
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: in 2024 to 64.86 billion in 2025. The growth was primarily driven by STL which increased by 11.99

asr-000126
00:15:23.839 --> 00:15:29.440
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: percent and the National Instant Sweepstakes Program, which grew by 20 percent. For the first

asr-000127
00:15:29.440 --> 00:15:39.440
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: semester of 2026, PCSO generated 32.68 billion. Overall, the revenue trend remains positive and

asr-000128
00:15:39.440 --> 00:15:48.399
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: resilient with STL serving as the main growth driver. The next slide reflects the comparative

asr-000129
00:15:48.399 --> 00:15:54.720
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: gross sales for the first semester of 2024 to the first semester of 2026.

asr-000130
00:15:54.720 --> 00:16:01.680
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: The graph shows a consistent upward trend in PCSO revenues for the first semester of 2024

asr-000131
00:16:01.680 --> 00:16:12.160
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: to 2026. Revenue increased from 30.98 billion in the first semester of 2024 to 31.89 billion in

asr-000132
00:16:12.160 --> 00:16:22.720
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: 2025, or 2.94 percent growth. This further increased to 32.68 billion in the first semester of 2026,

asr-000134
00:16:22.720 --> 00:16:45.440
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: representing another 2.48 percent increase. Overall, first-semester revenues grew by approximately 5.49 percent from 2024 to 2026. The next slide shows the comparative financial statements for 2024, 2025, and the first

asr-000135
00:16:45.440 --> 00:16:54.160
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: semester of 2026. The financial data show the total income increased by 3.86 percent

asr-000137
00:16:54.160 --> 00:17:05.520
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: from 63.42 billion in 2024 to 65.87 billion in 2025, indicating continued growth in revenues.

asr-000138
00:17:05.520 --> 00:17:16.640
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: However, operating expenses increased by 5.59%, from 51.01 billion to 53.86 billion.

asr-000139
00:17:16.640 --> 00:17:27.679
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: As a result, profit after tax likewise declined by 1.88%, from 11.74 billion to 11.52 billion.

asr-000140
00:17:27.679 --> 00:17:45.840
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: Financial assistance, subsidies, and contributions increased significantly by 20.84%, from 7.89 billion to 9.54 billion, reflecting the continued commitment to PCSO's charitable mandate.

asr-000141
00:17:45.840 --> 00:17:46.960
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: This contributed to

asr-000142
00:17:46.960 --> 00:17:59.679
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: the decline in net income, which decreased by 48.57%, from 3.84 billion in 2024 to 1.98 billion in 2025.

asr-000143
00:17:59.679 --> 00:18:13.919
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: As of June 30, 2026, PCSO already recorded 31.74 billion in total income and 3.35 billion in net income.

asr-000144
00:18:13.919 --> 00:18:22.559
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: The next slide illustrates the comparative financial statement.

asr-000145
00:18:22.559 --> 00:18:34.799
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: For the first semester of 2026, total income slightly decreased by 1.95%, from 32.38 billion to 31.74 billion.

asr-000146
00:18:34.799 --> 00:18:44.960
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: However, total expenses decreased by 6.95%, from 25.15 billion to 23.40 billion.

asr-000149
