asr-000189
00:23:14.400 --> 00:23:19.760
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: We now proceed to the significant accomplishments of PCSO

asr-000190
00:23:19.760 --> 00:23:23.919
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: for the year 2025 and the first semester of 2026,

asr-000191
00:23:23.919 --> 00:23:28.799
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: highlighting actual performance against planned targets.

asr-000192
00:23:28.799 --> 00:23:34.559
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: This covers five key areas, gross revenues, PTV distribution,

asr-000193
00:23:34.559 --> 00:23:40.799
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: medical assistance, institutional partnerships, and WLA certification.

asr-000194
00:23:40.799 --> 00:23:48.480
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: First, on gross revenues, in 2025, PCSO targeted 68.64 billion

asr-000195
00:23:48.480 --> 00:23:55.039
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: and achieved 64.86 billion, or 94.5% of the target.

asr-000196
00:23:55.039 --> 00:24:00.720
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: The shortfall was largely due to opportunity losses arising from several calamities

asr-000197
00:24:00.720 --> 00:24:04.320
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: and weather disturbances throughout 2025,

asr-000198
00:24:04.320 --> 00:24:09.600
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: which affected gaming operations and revenue-generating activities.

asr-000199
00:24:09.600 --> 00:24:11.039
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: Second, for PTV,

asr-000200
00:24:11.039 --> 00:24:19.600
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: distribution, PCSO significantly exceeded its 2025 target of 500 patient transport vehicles,

asr-000201
00:24:19.600 --> 00:24:25.840
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: distributing 1,090 PTVs, or 218% of target.

asr-000202
00:24:25.840 --> 00:24:32.559
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: For 2026, against a target of 258 PTVs,

asr-000203
00:24:32.559 --> 00:24:39.440
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: 154 PTVs have already been distributed as of July 31, 2026.

asr-000204
00:24:39.440 --> 00:24:42.720
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: Third, for the medical assistance,

asr-000205
00:24:42.720 --> 00:24:52.960
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: PCSO targeted 3.302 billion in 2025 and released 3.245 billion,

asr-000206
00:24:52.960 --> 00:25:03.039
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: benefiting 236,217 patients, or approximately 98.3% of the annual financial target.

asr-000207
00:25:03.039 --> 00:25:09.919
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: The slight shortfall reflects the timing and actual utilization of assistance during the year.

asr-000208
00:25:09.919 --> 00:25:11.360
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: For 2026,

asr-000209
00:25:11.360 --> 00:25:17.440
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: PCSO has allocated 3.65 billion for the medical assistance program.

asr-000210
00:25:17.440 --> 00:25:20.400
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: As of June 30, 2026,

asr-000211
00:25:20.400 --> 00:25:23.679
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: 1.64 billion has already been released,

asr-000212
00:25:23.679 --> 00:25:28.400
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: benefiting 118,400 patients.

asr-000213
00:25:28.400 --> 00:25:31.120
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: For the institutional partnership program,

asr-000214
00:25:31.120 --> 00:25:36.480
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: PCSO exceeded its 2025 target of 30 partner agencies

asr-000215
00:25:36.480 --> 00:25:40.559
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: by establishing partnerships with 38 agencies.

asr-000216
00:25:40.559 --> 00:25:42.480
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: For 2026,

asr-000217
00:25:42.480 --> 00:25:45.039
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: 19 partner agencies have already been

asr-000218
00:25:45.039 --> 00:25:47.840
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: established against the annual target of

asr-000219
00:25:47.840 --> 00:25:51.200
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: 30, representing 63% of the target

asr-000220
00:25:51.200 --> 00:25:53.679
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: as of the reporting period.

asr-000221
00:25:53.679 --> 00:25:56.640
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: Finally, for the World Lottery Association

asr-000222
00:25:56.640 --> 00:25:59.760
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: certifications, PCSO successfully

asr-000233
00:25:59.760 --> 00:26:07.679
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: attained World Lottery Association Level 3 Responsible Gaming Certification in 2025,

asr-000234
00:26:07.679 --> 00:26:11.520
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: exceeding its target of obtaining Level 3 certification.

asr-000235
00:26:11.520 --> 00:26:21.760
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: Responsible Gaming ensures that revenue generation is pursued in a manner that is ethical, sustainable, and socially responsible.

asr-000236
00:26:21.760 --> 00:26:32.720
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: For 2026, PCSO is pursuing World Lottery Association Security Control Standard 2024 Level 1 Certification,

asr-000237
00:26:32.720 --> 00:26:45.200
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: which focuses on strengthening the security and integrity of the corporation's system, information, critical operations, and security controls.

asr-000238
00:26:45.200 --> 00:26:53.440
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: We now move on to the other significant accomplishments of PCSO for the year 2025 and the first semester of 2026.

asr-000239
00:26:53.440 --> 00:27:02.400
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: First is a 100% distribution of patient transport vehicles to provinces, cities, and municipalities.

asr-000240
00:27:02.400 --> 00:27:18.320
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: Second is the donation of portable, AI-capable x-ray machines and various medical equipment to beneficiary entities amounting to P176 million.

asr-000241
00:27:18.320 --> 00:27:26.960
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: And the distribution of charity mobility aids, assistive devices, rescue devices, and evacuation kits

asr-000242
00:27:26.960 --> 00:27:38.400
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: to various LGUs amounting to P348.6 million under the Corporate Social Responsibility Program.

asr-000243
00:27:38.400 --> 00:27:49.919
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: We now go to the status of PCSO's remittances under the Universal Healthcare Program covering 2025 to the first semester of 2026.

asr-000245
00:27:49.919 --> 00:27:58.159
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: For 2025, PCSO remitted a total amount of approximately 2.57 billion.

asr-000246
00:27:58.159 --> 00:28:11.279
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: For 2026, covering the first two quarters, first quarter is 651.47 million and second quarter is 690.67 million.

asr-000247
00:28:11.279 --> 00:28:23.440
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: Combining 2025 remittances and the first semester of 2026, the total amount due and remitted is 3.914 billion pesos.

asr-000248
00:28:23.440 --> 00:28:38.320
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: It is important to highlight that the amount due and the amount remitted are exactly the same for each period, indicating 100% remittance of the amounts reflected in the table.

asr-000249
00:28:38.320 --> 00:28:54.159
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: For the next slide, we present PCSO's contribution to the National Treasury through taxes, dividends, and other remittances covering the period 2021 to the first semester of 2026.

asr-000250
00:28:54.159 --> 00:29:09.919
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: This table shows PCSO's contributions to the National Treasury through taxes, dividends, and mandatory contributions from 2021 to 2025, with the first semester of 2026 also reflected.

asr-000251
00:29:09.919 --> 00:29:24.320
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: For the last full five years, 2021 to 2025, PCSO contributed a total of approximately 101.29 billion to the National Government.

asr-000253
00:29:24.320 --> 00:29:40.559
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: Taxes accounted for the largest share at 79.04 billion, followed by dividends of 9.93 billion and universal healthcare contributions of 9.53 billion.

asr-000254
00:29:40.559 --> 00:29:53.200
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: Overall, PCSO's total contributions increased from 14.56 billion in 2021 to 21.85 billion in 2025.

asr-000256
00:29:53.200 --> 00:29:56.559
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: representing a 50.1% increase.

asr-000257
00:29:56.559 --> 00:29:59.919
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: As of June 30, 2026,

asr-000258
00:29:59.919 --> 00:30:07.360
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: PCSO has already remitted an additional 11.06 billion, bringing the total contributions

asr-000259
00:30:07.360 --> 00:30:15.840
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: reflected in the table to 112.35 billion. These figures demonstrate PCSO's significant

asr-000260
00:30:15.840 --> 00:30:22.799
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: and sustained contribution to government revenues, healthcare, and national programs.

asr-000261
00:30:22.799 --> 00:30:29.840
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: In closing, our report demonstrates PCSO's continued financial resilience, operating

asr-000262
00:30:29.840 --> 00:30:36.000
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: performance, and commitment to its charitable mandate. Despite changing economic conditions,

asr-000263
00:30:36.000 --> 00:30:41.840
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: PCSO continues to generate revenues, provide support for the health and welfare of the

asr-000264
00:30:41.840 --> 00:30:46.669
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: Filipino people, and contribute significantly to the national government.

asr-000265
00:30:46.669 --> 00:30:51.919
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: Sa bawat taya, may kawanggawa, and that is the greater purpose of

asr-000266
00:30:51.919 --> 00:30:52.838
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: PCSO.

asr-000267
00:30:53.600 --> 00:30:59.919
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: To transform hope into help, to turn revenues into meaningful assistance, and to ensure

asr-000268
00:30:59.919 --> 00:31:04.229
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: that the benefits of charity reach those who need them most.

asr-000269
00:31:04.559 --> 00:31:08.718
PCSO Corporate Planning Department Manager Atty. Anna Liza P. Inciong: PCSO hindi umu-urong sa pagtulong. Maraming salamat.

asr-000270
00:31:10.399 --> 00:31:16.799
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Thank you very much, Attorney Anna Liza P. Inciong, for your presentation.

asr-000271
00:31:16.799 --> 00:31:22.080
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Dear colleagues, before we begin, may I remind our distinguished guests

asr-000272
00:31:22.080 --> 00:31:29.039
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: and colleagues that each member is given five minutes for questioning or interpellation,

asr-000273
00:31:29.039 --> 00:31:41.440
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: excluding the response of the resource person. And when you hear the bell sound, it means

asr-000274
00:31:41.440 --> 00:31:50.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: you only have 30 seconds to wind up with your questions. As part of a long-standing and

asr-000275
00:31:50.000 --> 00:31:53.760
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: respected tradition of the House of Representatives to

asr-000276
00:31:53.760 --> 00:31:56.640
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: accord preferential treatment to the minority

asr-000277
00:31:56.640 --> 00:32:05.200
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: member of the House, followed by the independent and the majority member, in an alternating

asr-000278
00:32:05.200 --> 00:32:14.559
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: manner. The Chair now recognizes from the— from the majority, dahil wala pa yung minority.

asr-000279
00:32:14.559 --> 00:32:19.200
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Chair, from the minority.

asr-000280
00:32:19.200 --> 00:32:27.760
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Ay, sorry. Dito na pala si Congresswoman Montes. Sorry, hindi ko na.

asr-000281
00:32:27.760 --> 00:32:32.960
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Thank you. Thank you for correcting me, Representative Montes.

asr-000282
00:32:32.960 --> 00:32:40.480
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: So following our time-honored tradition, I now recognize Congresswoman Montes.

asr-000283
00:32:40.480 --> 00:32:43.440
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Thank you very much, Mr. Chair.

asr-000284
00:32:43.440 --> 00:32:55.360
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: My question is about UHC. RA11223, or the Universal Health Care Act, was enacted on Feb 20, 2019.

asr-000285
00:32:55.360 --> 00:33:05.617
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: And one of the provisions said that one year following its enactment,

asr-000286
00:33:05.617 --> 00:33:09.341
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: PCSO must remit the provision that 40% of the total health care costs

asr-000287
00:33:09.341 --> 00:33:11.919
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: should be allocated to the public health care system.

asr-000288
00:33:11.919 --> 00:33:19.760
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: And 40% of its net charity fund be given to the PhilHealth, for UHC.

asr-000289
00:33:19.760 --> 00:33:27.120
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: My question is, when did PCSO start remitting to the Bureau of Treasury?

asr-000290
00:33:27.120 --> 00:33:36.320
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: What year did it start?

asr-000291
00:33:36.320 --> 00:33:46.000
PCSO Chairperson Judge Felix P. Reyes: Our remittances to the PhilHealth at National Treasury or the UHC started way back in 2022.

asr-000292
00:33:46.000 --> 00:33:48.000
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Is my figure correct?

asr-000293
00:33:48.000 --> 00:33:59.600
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: So you started in 2022 with 2.71 billion, 2023, 2 billion, 2024, 2.13, 2025, 2.87, and two quarters.

asr-000294
00:33:59.600 --> 00:34:05.200
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Our first half of 2026, 194, based on the presentation, because it's 25 and 26.

asr-000295
00:34:05.200 --> 00:34:06.799
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Is that correct?

asr-000296
00:34:06.799 --> 00:34:11.760
PCSO Chairperson Judge Felix P. Reyes: Yes. Yes, Your Honor.

asr-000297
00:34:11.760 --> 00:34:15.599
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: My question is, were these remittances made on time?

asr-000298
00:34:15.599 --> 00:34:17.679
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Meaning, as per the provision of...

asr-000299
00:34:17.679 --> 00:34:22.159
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: As per the law, it has to be quarterly, the remittance.

asr-000300
00:34:22.159 --> 00:34:25.359
PCSO Chairperson Judge Felix P. Reyes: Yes, we are doing it on time, quarterly.

asr-000301
00:34:25.359 --> 00:34:31.040
PCSO Chairperson Judge Felix P. Reyes: And for the last time, our GM even personally delivered it to the National Treasury.

asr-000302
00:34:31.040 --> 00:34:34.720
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: There were never an instance that it was delayed, Mr. Chair?

asr-000303
00:34:34.720 --> 00:34:37.200
PCSO Chairperson Judge Felix P. Reyes: None that we remember, Your Honor.

asr-000304
00:34:37.200 --> 00:34:39.520
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Okay.

asr-000305
00:34:39.520 --> 00:34:48.240
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: From what I understand, on July 16, you turned over, among other contributions of people,

asr-000306
00:34:48.240 --> 00:34:57.600
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: PCSO to the National Government, you turned over to the Bureau of Treasury.

asr-000307
00:34:57.600 --> 00:35:12.079
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: The 1.935 billion that you turned over covers mandatory contributions from 4th quarter 2025 through 1st quarter and 2nd quarter 2026.

asr-000308
00:35:12.079 --> 00:35:26.240
